    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the **salutation** feature on the `POST /api/owners` + `GET /api/owners/{id}` flow, following the codebase's established pattern for owner fields (declare in the OpenAPI spec \u2192 DTOs regenerate \u2192 MapStruct maps by name \u2192 derived `@Transient` getter on the entity).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`**\n   - Added an optional `title` input property to `OwnerFields` (enum `MR`/`MRS`/`MS`/`DR`, matching the spec's stated values).\n   - Added a read-only, derived `salutation` property to `Owner`.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`**\n   - Added a persisted `title` column (`@Column(name = \"title\")`) with getter/setter.\n   - Added a `@Transient getSalutation()`: returns `title + \" \" + lastName` when a title is present, otherwise just `lastName` \u2014 consistent with the other derived getters (`getDisplayName`, `getInitials`, etc.).\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `title` column to the `owners` table so the value persists and reads back on `GET`.\n\nThe generated `OwnerMapperImpl` correctly round-trips the enum\u2194String (`title`) and populates `salutation` from `owner.getSalutation()`. No application code in the controller needed changing \u2014 the create flow maps `title` from the request onto the owner, and the derived `salutation` flows into the response automatically. The acceptance test `coreComposesSalutation` (title `DR`, lastName `who` \u2192 `salutation` = `\"DR who\"`) passes.",
